@startuml
title Unified Current History and Backfill Sync
start
:Run one scheduled slot (2.2 second fixed delay);
if (facility lookup due?) then (yes)
  :Call /carpark and cache allowed facility IDs/names;
else (no)
  :Choose current-date refresh or older-date backfill work;
  :Call /carpark/history once for facility and date;
endif
if (request successful?) then (yes)
  :Convert Sydney MessageDate values to UTC Instants;
  :Upsert newest sample per ten-minute Sydney bucket;
  :Set the same ParkingDay state COMPLETE;
  note right: Today’s response supplies the live chart tail and history.
else (no)
  :Set the same ParkingDay state RETRY_WAIT;
  :Record retryAfter;
endif
:Return;
stop

note right
  A single scheduled loop calls the history endpoint for every date,
  including today. The current-date response is also the live update;
  there is no separate live data request or polling path.

  The compound key is (facilityId, sydneyDate). The daily record stores
  bounded samples and durable backfill status together. Missing means
  not fetched; PROCESSING uses leaseUntil, RETRY_WAIT uses retryAfter,
  and COMPLETE (including an empty result) is skipped for backfill.
  Current-date polling continues after COMPLETE so its live tail stays fresh.

  Four of every five history work slots rotate through facilities for
  today's date; every fifth slot selects the newest eligible older date.
  Facility lookup refreshes consume a loop slot. Total provider traffic
  stays under 39,273 calls/day and below 1 call per 2 seconds, including
  cold start and initial backfill.
  If a worker fails after sample upsert, retrying is safe.
end note
@enduml
